  "validation_finished_at": "2026-11-15T03:07:00Z",
  "body": "Gymnasium's [TimeLimit](https://github.com/Farama-Foundation/Gymnasium/blob/v1.1.1/gymnasium/wrappers/common.py) can report termination and truncation on the same step. With time-limit bootstrapping enabled, the agents currently add a continuation value whenever truncated is true, including transitions that have actually terminated. That inflates the terminal value target: with reward 1, discount 0.5, and a critic value of 10, the target becomes 6 instead of 1.\n\nGate the truncation bootstrap on `truncated & ~terminated` across the Torch and JAX on-policy agents, including recurrent variants and IPPO/MAPPO. Apply the same condition in the Warp PPO kernel. The existing GAE episode-boundary handling is preserved.\n\nRegression coverage checks all four flag combinations, enabled/disabled bootstrapping, and JAX boolean/int8 signals through the public agent APIs. A real Gymnasium TimeLimit regression runs PPO.post_interaction and verifies both the resulting returns and a finite critic parameter update.\n\nValidation: [CPU verification run](https://github.com/Afloat16/skrl/actions/runs/43670074588).\n\n- Unchanged source: 12 Torch, 10 JAX, and 1 Warp regression failures; all disabled-bootstrap controls pass.\n- Corrected public API regressions: 46 pass.\n- Complete CPU agent suites: Torch 91 pass, JAX 48 pass, Warp 10 pass. The 103 CUDA-parameterized cases are deselected.\n- Repository pre-commit hooks pass, including Black, isort, and Pyright.\n\nTested on Python 3.12.3, Torch 2.6.0+cpu, JAX 0.4.35 / Flax 0.10.2, and Warp 1.15.0 / warp-nn 0.4.1.\n",
  "prefilled_url": "https://github.com/Toni-SM/skrl/compare/develop...Afloat16:skrl:fix/terminal-time-limit-bootstrap-20261115?expand=1&title=Exclude%20terminal%20states%20from%20truncation%20bootstrap&body=Gymnasium's%20%5BTimeLimit%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FFarama-Foundation%2FGymnasium%2Fblob%2Fv1.1.1%2Fgymnasium%2Fwrappers%2Fcommon.py)%20can%20report%20termination%20and%20truncation%20on%20the%20same%20step.%20With%20time-limit%20bootstrapping%20enabled%2C%20the%20agents%20currently%20add%20a%20continuation%20value%20whenever%20truncated%20is%20true%2C%20including%20transitions%20that%20have%20actually%20terminated.%20That%20inflates%20the%20terminal%20value%20target%3A%20with%20reward%201%2C%20discount%200.5%2C%20and%20a%20critic%20value%20of%2010%2C%20the%20target%20becomes%206%20instead%20of%201.%0A%0AGate%20the%20truncation%20bootstrap%20on%20%60truncated%20%26%20~terminated%60%20across%20the%20Torch%20and%20JAX%20on-policy%20agents%2C%20including%20recurrent%20variants%20and%20IPPO%2FMAPPO.%20Apply%20the%20same%20condition%20in%20the%20Warp%20PPO%20kernel.%20The%20existing%20GAE%20episode-boundary%20handling%20is%20preserved.%0A%0ARegression%20coverage%20checks%20all%20four%20flag%20combinations%2C%20enabled%2Fdisabled%20bootstrapping%2C%20and%20JAX%20boolean%2Fint8%20signals%20through%20the%20public%20agent%20APIs.%20A%20real%20Gymnasium%20TimeLimit%20regression%20runs%20PPO.post_interaction%20and%20verifies%20both%20the%20resulting%20returns%20and%20a%20finite%20critic%20parameter%20update.%0A%0AValidation%3A%20%5BCPU%20verification%20run%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FAfloat16%2Fskrl%2Factions%2Fruns%2F43670074588).%0A%0A-%20Unchanged%20source%3A%2012%20Torch%2C%2010%20JAX%2C%20and%201%20Warp%20regression%20failures%3B%20all%20disabled-bootstrap%20controls%20pass.%0A-%20Corrected%20public%20API%20regressions%3A%2046%20pass.%0A-%20Complete%20CPU%20agent%20suites%3A%20Torch%2091%20pass%2C%20JAX%2048%20pass%2C%20Warp%2010%20pass.%20The%20103%20CUDA-parameterized%20cases%20are%20deselected.%0A-%20Repository%20pre-commit%20hooks%20pass%2C%20including%20Black%2C%20isort%2C%20and%20Pyright.%0A%0ATested%20on%20Python%203.12.3%2C%20Torch%202.6.0%2Bcpu%2C%20JAX%200.4.35%20%2F%20Flax%200.10.2%2C%20and%20Warp%201.15.0%20%2F%20warp-nn%200.4.1.%0A",
